PATCH 642: carry actual detail FILEMGR results into the engine effects input (board:0014).

Original7660/6032 returns full EAX/EBX through0f57/0f5d/e339/de89. The source
normal result is EAX804/EBX5, produced by the real file read/close, not a fixed
handle or upper-word policy. Hand-written op44 publishes those actual return
lanes once; retain the existing void de89 and generic gateway signatures.
6de2 consumes that typed result after de89, retaining EBX across the realc008.
Original6e05 MOV AX,[8b4b] and6e08 SHR AX,1 load the second independent config
WORD. Preserve EAX's high WORD as the original MOV AX does; pass full EAX and
full EBX separately into e2df instead of its stale pre-de89 parameter. e2df
publishes its explicit EAX input before its actual task-inbox/selector/callback
sequence. The shim includes both lanes in its existing transparent ISR saves.

Sources: detail_return_case.json and detail_return_state_case.json; complete
original89-fetch trace,25 full GP/segment/raw+lazyflag/control/time/16MiB
boundaries and23 exact instruction/RAM transitions. Kernel image6032/7660,
engine image6de2/de89/e339/e2df constrain the register and WORD contracts.

The regression executes real ordered-patched6de2/de89/e339/c008/e2df and the
actual op44 branch/6032/DOS against isolated original detail tables. Eight
parent target failures become eight cases; real extra DOS peer opens retain
handles5..7 while detail close returns6..8, proving the result is not fitted5.
Full guarded table bytes and actual DOS commands remain checked. Independent
WORD configs include0/2/4 and values with the high bit set. The observer stops
at the actual op68 gateway input without inventing the effects handler/return.
This accepts normal EAX/EBX/configuration data transport only. Complete incoming
GP, flags, segments/stack, nonlocal error continuation, op68/77e2 device/IRQ
execution, instruction/device time and full frame/mixed PCM parity remain open.
